# This repository commits generated artifacts (erd.py, docs/index.html, the
# examples/showcase/output tree) and its drift checks compare them to freshly
# regenerated output BYTE FOR BYTE. That only holds if Git hands every checkout
# the same bytes that were committed, so line-ending translation has to be off
# everywhere. Without this file, Git on Windows checks the committed LF files
# out as CRLF, the generator writes LF (cli.py forces newline=''), and the
# drift checks fail on Windows alone while passing on Linux.
#
# No file here needs CRLF — the repository ships no .bat, .cmd or .ps1.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compared byte for byte by the showcase drift checks, so never let the text
# heuristics near them: .xlsx is a ZIP and .db is a SQLite database.
*.png  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.xlsx binary
*.db   binary
